<main>
  <div class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">OpenStrongman</p>
    <h1>Research Roadmap</h1>
    <p>What strongman science knows, what it doesn't, and which open questions this dataset can help answer.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rm-wrap">

    <section class="rm-section">
      <h2>How this roadmap works</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Strongman is one of the least studied strength sports. Only a few dozen peer-reviewed papers deal with it, and many of those recruited rugby players or recreational lifters rather than strongman competitors. This page maps what is known, names what is not, and points to the work that would close each gap.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        The structure is borrowed from NASA's <a href="https://humanresearchroadmap.nasa.gov/intro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Human Research Roadmap</a>,<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-1">1</a></sup> which organizes spaceflight health research into risks, the knowledge gaps inside each risk, and the tasks that would close them. NASA rates each risk by likelihood and consequence. We don't have the data to do that honestly yet, so each risk area here is rated by how much strongman-specific evidence exists instead.
      </p>

      <div class="structure" aria-label="Roadmap structure: Risk, then Gap, then Task">
        <div class="structure-step">
          <p class="step-label">1 &middot; Risk</p>
          <h3>A broad area of concern</h3>
          <p>A health or performance problem the sport faces, such as injury or drug use, with a summary of the published evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="structure-step">
          <p class="step-label">2 &middot; Gap</p>
          <h3>A specific open question</h3>
          <p>Something we would need to know to reduce that risk. Each gap has a permanent ID, like INJ-2, that you can cite or link to.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="structure-step">
          <p class="step-label">3 &middot; Task</p>
          <h3>The work that closes it</h3>
          <p>A study, dataset, or schema change. Tasks are tagged by whether OpenStrongman data can do the job or outside research is needed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rm-section">
      <div class="key-box" role="note" aria-label="Key">
        <span class="key-head">Evidence</span>
        <div class="key-row">
          <span class="key-item"><span class="ev ev-none">None</span> no strongman-specific study found</span>
          <span class="key-item"><span class="ev ev-minimal">Minimal</span> one or two descriptive studies</span>
          <span class="key-item"><span class="ev ev-limited">Limited</span> surveys, case reports, or small samples only</span>
          <span class="key-item"><span class="ev ev-developing">Developing</span> includes lab or controlled studies</span>
        </div>
        <span class="key-head">Task path</span>
        <div class="key-row">
          <span class="key-item"><span class="path path-osm">OpenStrongman data</span> answerable with current fields as coverage grows</span>
          <span class="key-item"><span class="path path-field">New field needed</span> needs a proposed schema addition</span>
          <span class="key-item"><span class="path path-external">Outside research</span> needs lab, clinical, or survey data</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div id="roadmap-root">
      <p class="lede" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--faint);">Loading roadmap...</p>
    </div>

    <section class="rm-section" id="fields-section" hidden>
      <h2>Proposed schema additions</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Several gaps can't be closed with the current columns. These fields are proposals drawn from the roadmap, not adopted changes. Each would need a schema decision before it is added to the data.
      </p>
      <div class="data-table-wrap">
        <table class="data-table field-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Proposed field</th><th>Would help close</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="fields-body"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rm-section">
      <div class="contribute-box">
        <h3>Working on one of these questions?</h3>
        <p>
          If you are a researcher, clinician, coach, or student planning a study that touches a gap on this page, we want to hear about it. Open an issue on the <a href="https://github.com/campoheidi-oss/openstrongman.org/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a> and include the gap ID in the title. Every gap on this page has its own link for starting that conversation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Published a paper we missed, or think a gap is framed wrong? Tell us the same way. This roadmap will be revised as the evidence changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="references-section">
      <h2>Method and references</h2>
      <p class="method" id="method-note"></p>
      <ol id="ref-list"></ol>
      <p class="method" style="margin-top:1rem;">OpenStrongman is not affiliated with NASA. The Human Research Roadmap is used here as a structural model only.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
